WEBVTT

01:04.064 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:18.411 --> 01:20.789
Hello. Hi.

01:23.166 --> 01:24.334
Wow, you look beautiful.

01:24.417 --> 01:25.919
Could you help me? Oh my.

01:26.002 --> 01:27.128
Well done.

01:27.212 --> 01:28.797
-Help me with this.
-Okay.

01:37.555 --> 01:38.431
Here we go.

01:38.515 --> 01:39.474
YALASHANG FILM CLUB

01:39.974 --> 01:41.476
One, two, three.

01:43.394 --> 01:46.231
I'll take one more.

01:47.107 --> 01:48.108
Smile.

01:49.109 --> 01:50.610
One, two, three!

01:53.738 --> 01:55.657
What does it mean if I can't go?

01:56.282 --> 01:59.160
Tonight… is our last night.

02:00.745 --> 02:02.789
Our last night before you join the army!

02:05.875 --> 02:07.585
Do I really have to…

02:07.669 --> 02:09.045
What's wrong with you?

02:35.029 --> 02:37.157
Hey, who knows what will happen?

02:37.824 --> 02:40.618
They say you don't know
until you walk down the aisle.

02:41.828 --> 02:44.831
Just wait and see.
I'll see you in a wedding dress.

02:45.456 --> 02:46.791
Ta-da!

02:46.875 --> 02:48.042
It's so beautiful.

02:55.508 --> 02:57.218
I should cover this up.

03:00.597 --> 03:01.806
I kept my promise.

03:02.307 --> 03:04.434
Oh? Hey, over here.

03:04.517 --> 03:05.351
Hey!

03:06.978 --> 03:09.939
Not knowing who might come back
or come anew,

03:10.023 --> 03:11.024
my heart pounded…

03:13.902 --> 03:14.986
Oh my!

03:17.197 --> 03:18.948
I didn't pop it on purpose.

03:20.658 --> 03:23.536
…and my feet felt like they were floating.

03:27.749 --> 03:30.835
SUCH AN UNEVEN LOVE

03:35.381 --> 03:38.218
A new person has also
come into my mom's world.

03:39.677 --> 03:42.430
A squishy thing that claims to be human.

03:42.931 --> 03:46.517
HAPPY FIRST BIRTHDAY
FROM YEOM BYEONG-CHEOL, NA MIN-OK

04:04.410 --> 04:06.537
Evoking unexpectedly deep affection

04:06.621 --> 04:08.498
despite being two generations apart,

04:09.624 --> 04:12.085
an endearing monster has come the world.

04:12.752 --> 04:15.546
Don't babysit your grandkid,
no matter how adorable.

04:16.047 --> 04:18.883
They're even more adorable
when you only see them occasionally.

04:18.967 --> 04:22.512
Once Geum-myeong gets married,
throw off the burden of parenting.

04:22.595 --> 04:24.305
Live carefree and soar free.

04:26.349 --> 04:30.019
Everyone says the kid has my eyes,
but the trap is from his mother's--

04:30.103 --> 04:31.479
The jaw area.

04:35.817 --> 04:38.778
What about your family?
Aren't they coming?

04:40.405 --> 04:41.489
Well, you know…

04:41.572 --> 04:43.616
I wouldn't take an unemployed son-in-law.

04:46.494 --> 04:48.329
Well, what about your brothers?

04:50.081 --> 04:50.915
They just said

04:51.874 --> 04:53.626
they better not see our asses again.

04:55.211 --> 04:56.796
-Faces.
-Sorry?

04:58.423 --> 04:59.507
Faces.

05:02.969 --> 05:05.054
-Feces?
-Faces!

05:07.056 --> 05:08.057
Faces.

05:13.313 --> 05:14.814
That's 19 grams.

05:15.398 --> 05:18.568
Goodness, they mentioned "19 grams"
on the phone a dozen times.

05:18.651 --> 05:20.486
They told me to go to college with it.

05:21.195 --> 05:25.283
Goodness, that stingy old man.
Hasn't he heard of inflation?

05:25.366 --> 05:28.828
He should pay the market rate for college.
They have money, don't they?

05:29.996 --> 05:32.206
He got this for us by selling rice cakes?

05:32.290 --> 05:33.249
Yes.

05:33.333 --> 05:35.126
This grandpa drives a Mercedes, right?

05:35.209 --> 05:38.087
Of course he does.
Everyone eats rice cakes.

05:42.050 --> 05:43.634
Not a cool job though.

05:44.135 --> 05:45.511
"Cool"?

05:48.973 --> 05:49.974
Let's go.

05:53.144 --> 05:55.063
YANG CHE-IL'S FIRST BIRTHDAY

05:55.563 --> 05:57.607
Should you be spending on that now?

06:00.651 --> 06:02.278
I'm going to do everything for him.

06:02.779 --> 06:04.655
You always just got by on my birthday.

06:04.739 --> 06:07.075
-At the time, it was all we--
-I'm sure.

06:07.158 --> 06:08.451
It was only tough on mine.

06:09.160 --> 06:12.538
How will you support your family now?
Planning to live with us forever?

06:12.622 --> 06:14.957
-I'm working on a business plan.
-Business?

06:15.541 --> 06:16.459
With Cheol-yong?

06:16.542 --> 06:18.294
I told you not to run a pawnshop.

06:18.378 --> 06:20.129
Life is all about the lucky strike--

06:20.213 --> 06:22.632
I should just strike you, damn it.

06:22.715 --> 06:25.760
Others mature when they have a family.
Why are you chasing empty--

06:25.843 --> 06:27.011
I don't need your help.

06:27.095 --> 06:29.138
Am I expecting much from you?

06:29.222 --> 06:31.391
Just get up early, for starters!

06:31.474 --> 06:33.434
Go to the loading docks or something.

06:33.518 --> 06:35.561
-And look for a job!
-Seriously.

06:37.188 --> 06:38.564
You want me to live like you?

06:39.357 --> 06:40.358
Is that what you want?

06:41.401 --> 06:42.276
Father.

06:42.360 --> 06:45.488
You have to open the faucet fully
to fill the bucket up.

06:45.571 --> 06:49.450
You get nowhere in life
trying to mend every leaking hole.

06:49.534 --> 06:50.368
You know it too.

06:50.952 --> 06:53.579
Don't just count on Geum-myeong.
Watch what I can do too!

06:53.663 --> 06:57.750
I won't be the dad who orders pork belly
for three when my family eats out.

06:57.834 --> 07:00.920
I'll be the dad
who orders five or six servings.

07:23.025 --> 07:24.944
Why are you like that to your father?

07:25.987 --> 07:29.365
Your heart softens as you age.
Even Steelheart gets scars.

07:32.160 --> 07:34.704
Then Geum-myeong's mom
can comfort Geum-myeong's father.

07:34.787 --> 07:35.621
Good grief.

07:36.497 --> 07:38.916
How do you keep getting more spiky?

07:39.625 --> 07:42.003
Frankly, you should be thankful
I've grown this much.

07:42.086 --> 07:43.713
Kids grow as much as you believe.

07:43.796 --> 07:46.466
Geum-myeong grew so much
because you believed in her fully.

07:46.549 --> 07:48.968
You only ever doubt me,
so I've only grown this much.

07:49.051 --> 07:50.595
You're unbelievable!

07:50.678 --> 07:53.806
Carry the baby already!
My arms are hurting.

07:54.682 --> 07:55.516
Goodness.

07:57.268 --> 08:00.521
Here, give me Che-il. You two go inside.
Hurry, hand him over to me.

08:01.647 --> 08:04.692
My sweet baby. Come here.

08:04.775 --> 08:06.235
My goodness.

08:23.127 --> 08:26.672
I really had no idea
my daughter would do this.

08:27.590 --> 08:29.425
I felt betrayed.

08:29.509 --> 08:31.552
I felt like my entire world fell apart.

08:32.261 --> 08:33.262
I can't tell you

08:34.263 --> 08:37.141
how sorry I am, and…

08:37.225 --> 08:39.602
Goodness, if you get married pregnant,

08:39.685 --> 08:43.314
you can't even get a brass ring,
let alone a gold one.

08:44.315 --> 08:46.484
I never even got to have a wedding.

08:46.984 --> 08:50.029
She won't ever get to wear a veil either.

08:51.155 --> 08:55.660
Eun-myeong may still be struggling
to find his way,

08:56.160 --> 08:57.537
but as a person--

08:57.620 --> 09:00.665
I have nothing against Eun-myeong.

09:02.250 --> 09:03.084
Why is that?

09:03.751 --> 09:06.379
They say sons take after their fathers.

09:07.171 --> 09:11.300
I've always envied your life
more than anyone else's.

09:13.135 --> 09:15.471
You're the wife of a rich family.

09:16.806 --> 09:18.307
On the kids' sports days,

09:19.267 --> 09:22.562
I dragged three kids along on my own
under the scorching sun.

09:23.312 --> 09:27.483
Then I saw your husband
fanning your back so you could cool off.

09:28.651 --> 09:32.780
You've always had a knack
for noticing things.

09:33.823 --> 09:34.949
It made me cry.

09:36.409 --> 09:39.745
I wondered how you were so blessed
to be treated so well

09:41.080 --> 09:45.084
and what sins I had committed
to step on such a pile of poop.

09:48.212 --> 09:49.130
So,

09:50.548 --> 09:51.882
is Hyeon-suk doing okay?

09:53.050 --> 09:55.177
She doesn't know how to do anything.

09:55.678 --> 09:57.972
Scold her if she doesn't know anything.

09:58.472 --> 10:00.933
Scold her until she cries her eyes out.

10:01.434 --> 10:02.810
I won't scold her.

10:02.893 --> 10:04.812
I won't make her cry her eyes out.

10:05.313 --> 10:08.524
I won't be giving Hyeon-suk a brass ring.

10:09.400 --> 10:10.234
Okay?

10:12.862 --> 10:15.615
If you want to see
your first grandson or Hyeon-suk,

10:17.325 --> 10:19.952
feel free to visit them whenever you want.

10:20.036 --> 10:21.329
Or call me to come out.

10:21.829 --> 10:25.791
We share our children,
so we're in this together, right?

10:28.586 --> 10:32.048
Goodness, how can he look
exactly like my daughter?

10:35.509 --> 10:36.427
Dear me.

10:37.762 --> 10:41.057
It seems like you can't win
against your daughter either.

10:43.643 --> 10:46.270
The title of a poem my mom once wrote…

10:48.856 --> 10:50.024
was "My Damn Child."

10:50.107 --> 10:51.651
What's the big deal?

10:51.734 --> 10:53.027
For crying out loud!

10:54.236 --> 10:55.780
You little punk!

10:57.490 --> 10:59.909
Is she off to save the country
or her company?

10:59.992 --> 11:03.079
Good grief. Just give it to me.

11:03.579 --> 11:05.581
Why buy Chivas
for a child's first birthday?

11:05.665 --> 11:07.792
Cheol-yong must be out of his mind.

11:07.875 --> 11:09.960
Because you and Dad look down on me,

11:10.044 --> 11:12.672
she treats her only nephew's
first birthday like this, huh?

11:13.673 --> 11:18.052
Your sister's having a rough time too.
Her company is also in deep trouble.

11:19.220 --> 11:22.139
She acts all high and mighty
because she works at a big company.

11:22.223 --> 11:25.601
But who takes care of you and Father?
Who'll care for you when you're sick?

11:25.685 --> 11:28.396
As if you could take care of anyone!

11:28.479 --> 11:32.108
Take care of yourself first. Yourself.

11:33.317 --> 11:36.404
Don't be so harsh.
Even a crooked tree shades the weary.

11:36.487 --> 11:40.324
The shock is even greater
as the rumors turn out to be true.

11:40.408 --> 11:43.411
This is likely to have
a deep, significant impact on our economy.

11:43.494 --> 11:45.162
Kwon Jae-hong reports.

11:45.246 --> 11:48.666
This afternoon, Korea First Bank,
Kia's main banking partner,

11:48.749 --> 11:52.920
announced at a press conference
that 18 of Kia Group's 28 subsidiaries…

11:53.003 --> 11:55.172
It was a season of reaping what was sown,

11:55.256 --> 11:56.632
whether it was a gold toad…

11:59.719 --> 12:00.886
or a postdated check.

12:48.517 --> 12:51.145
-Stop layoffs right now!
-Stop layoffs!

12:51.228 --> 12:55.107
-We won't just leave like this!
-We won't!

12:55.191 --> 12:58.819
-Stop layoffs right now!
-Stop layoffs!

12:58.903 --> 13:02.531
-We won't just leave like this!
-We won't!

13:02.615 --> 13:05.117
The Asian financial crisis
is dismantling corporations,

13:05.201 --> 13:07.328
triggering widespread unemployment.

13:07.411 --> 13:09.121
OVERSEAS BUSINESS DIVISION
ASSISTANT MANAGER

13:09.789 --> 13:13.334
A particularly unforgettable winter
was on its way.

13:13.417 --> 13:15.419
Dainong Group, the 34th largest company,

13:15.503 --> 13:18.589
has effectively been dissolved
except for the Midopa Company.

13:18.672 --> 13:22.635
Of the four subsidiaries subject
to protection, only Midopa was revived.

13:22.718 --> 13:24.887
While Dainong Ltd. went into receivership,

13:24.970 --> 13:26.889
Dainong Heavy Industries
and Metro Product…

13:26.972 --> 13:29.600
Anyone can get approved!
100% credit card approval!

13:29.683 --> 13:33.354
Ssangbangwool Development and Corporation,
which filed for composition yesterday,

13:33.437 --> 13:34.688
were declared bankrupt.

13:34.772 --> 13:36.565
Taeil, after financial struggles,

13:36.649 --> 13:39.985
was designated today
for bankruptcy protection.

13:40.528 --> 13:44.156
The debts of Taeil and its subsidiaries
totaled 970 billion won.

13:44.240 --> 13:46.992
Chohung Bank and other bond creditors
will meet on the 24th…

13:47.076 --> 13:49.245
Stocks have plunged again,
with KOSPI falling…

13:49.328 --> 13:51.705
First of all, thank you
for giving me the opportunity

13:51.789 --> 13:54.208
to be here in difficult times…

13:56.335 --> 13:57.336
First,

13:57.962 --> 14:03.592
thank you for the opportunity
to interview during this difficult time.

14:03.676 --> 14:05.135
I am willing to do…

14:05.219 --> 14:08.180
After barely holding on
through severe financial struggles,

14:08.264 --> 14:10.683
Haitai Group finally filed
for bankruptcy today.

14:11.183 --> 14:15.729
This toothpaste was exported
across Northeast Asia

14:16.313 --> 14:19.817
and was often unavailable
due to high demand,

14:20.317 --> 14:23.404
but due to the manufacturer's bankruptcy…

14:24.655 --> 14:26.323
This toothpaste alone fights

14:26.866 --> 14:27.700
common cavities

14:28.701 --> 14:29.869
and gum disease

14:30.452 --> 14:31.829
and whitens stained teeth.

14:32.329 --> 14:37.918
This product is the result
of a technical collaboration

14:38.419 --> 14:42.631
with an American toothpaste company
recognized by the WHO. And so…

14:42.715 --> 14:46.135
Newcore Group, the 25th largest company,
filed for composition

14:46.218 --> 14:48.220
and was declared bankrupt today.

14:48.304 --> 14:49.305
Dear viewers,

14:49.388 --> 14:54.310
the government has decided
to request a bailout from the IMF.

14:54.894 --> 14:57.646
Despite its reputation
for economic success,

14:57.730 --> 15:00.149
Korea has been forced
to admit national bankruptcy

15:00.232 --> 15:05.070
and seek recovery with assistance
from international organizations.

15:05.154 --> 15:08.073
The government aims
to minimize the IMF policy intervention,

15:08.157 --> 15:10.367
even if Korea receives its bailout funds.

15:10.451 --> 15:15.706
The next stop is Sillim Market,
formerly known as Cannes Theater.

15:16.874 --> 15:22.087
The next stop is Sillim Market,
formerly known as Cannes Theater.

15:42.066 --> 15:44.234
CANNES THEATER WILL SHUT DOWN
ON DECEMBER 1

15:44.693 --> 15:46.070
When one door closes…

15:48.072 --> 15:50.699
another is bound to creak open.

15:57.581 --> 15:59.708
TICKET, JA 17

16:09.760 --> 16:13.138
Hey, can't you just sit anywhere?

16:19.186 --> 16:20.688
JA 17

16:23.190 --> 16:26.110
This isn't a leg rest. It's an armrest.

16:26.694 --> 16:27.778
It's an armrest.

17:12.239 --> 17:15.784
You need countless lifetimes of fate
to meet even once in this life,

17:16.285 --> 17:18.787
so the third time should be the charm.

17:24.209 --> 17:25.669
Hey, did you see her?

17:26.837 --> 17:27.838
Did you meet her?

17:28.338 --> 17:29.882
-Sorry?
-You didn't see her?

17:31.050 --> 17:32.801
Who told you to clean up?

17:32.885 --> 17:36.555
I lined her up for you,
and you still missed the goal.

17:39.266 --> 17:40.768
If even the third time fails…

17:42.978 --> 17:44.730
you must wait for the next life.

17:44.813 --> 17:45.814
Geum-myeong!

17:58.952 --> 18:00.496
Last time, it was Seo Taiji.

18:02.289 --> 18:03.499
This time, it was H.O.T.

18:03.582 --> 18:04.833
Geum-myeong!

18:33.612 --> 18:34.446
Geum-myeong!

19:04.893 --> 19:06.520
Only then did he realize.

19:09.940 --> 19:11.650
You only get three chances.

19:12.526 --> 19:14.486
If no one scores in extra time,

19:15.696 --> 19:17.489
it will go to a penalty shootout.

19:39.803 --> 19:40.804
Stop!

19:43.265 --> 19:44.099
Sir!

19:44.183 --> 19:46.059
When one door closes,

19:46.143 --> 19:49.021
another is bound to creak open.

19:49.104 --> 19:50.814
Could've caught the next one.

19:51.440 --> 19:52.274
Goodness.

19:52.858 --> 19:53.859
Thank you.

20:12.669 --> 20:15.130
If the IMF crisis hadn't happened…

20:19.384 --> 20:21.011
If I hadn't lost my job…

20:26.391 --> 20:28.936
If the theater hadn't gone
out of business…

20:35.692 --> 20:39.154
If any of those gears had failed
to do their part…

20:46.286 --> 20:48.705
Everyone off. This is the last stop.

20:49.706 --> 20:52.876
…perhaps this moment
would never have happened.

21:00.217 --> 21:01.093
Is this a dream?

21:03.262 --> 21:04.096
Is it?

21:05.806 --> 21:06.974
Yes.

21:15.565 --> 21:18.151
I chased you from the theater.

21:19.194 --> 21:20.487
I ran like mad.

21:20.570 --> 21:24.825
I couldn't let you slip away,
even if it meant losing my breath.

21:28.036 --> 21:29.037
Were you

21:30.289 --> 21:31.415
alone at the theater?

21:32.749 --> 21:33.709
-Yes.
-I see.

21:37.838 --> 21:40.299
-Were you also--
-Yes.

21:46.346 --> 21:47.306
Finally.

21:48.098 --> 21:49.850
This is when we use

21:51.351 --> 21:52.644
the word "finally," right?

22:25.177 --> 22:27.471
Why do you keep laughing?

22:29.681 --> 22:32.642
You look totally different now.

22:33.143 --> 22:35.604
I guess you're not Picasso anymore.

22:35.687 --> 22:36.688
I am.

22:36.772 --> 22:40.108
I'm the Picasso
at a place called Picasso Art Academy.

22:42.819 --> 22:45.906
Our academy would be ruined without me.
They pay me well.

22:47.032 --> 22:48.408
It's just so great.

22:49.076 --> 22:49.993
Really.

22:52.371 --> 22:53.372
Me too.

22:54.873 --> 22:55.999
It's just so great.

23:01.546 --> 23:04.174
How did we both end up
at the theater today?

23:04.257 --> 23:06.176
I actually went every day.

23:07.344 --> 23:08.303
Just in case.

23:10.764 --> 23:11.890
I really missed you.

23:16.770 --> 23:17.896
I missed you a lot.

23:25.278 --> 23:26.113
So we can now…

23:27.072 --> 23:28.073
"Now"?

23:28.156 --> 23:29.991
Or shouldn't we?

23:32.577 --> 23:33.412
A lager, please.

23:33.495 --> 23:35.455
Still, we shouldn't?

23:37.332 --> 23:39.543
Oh, we can order alcohol now.

23:40.210 --> 23:41.586
Let's order beer.

23:41.670 --> 23:44.673
Just beer?

23:45.173 --> 23:46.758
JINRO SOJU

23:51.888 --> 23:52.889
Wait.

23:53.974 --> 23:57.352
Why do you keep staring?

23:58.562 --> 23:59.938
It's driving me crazy.

24:00.522 --> 24:01.356
I know, right?

24:02.232 --> 24:03.275
It's also

24:04.025 --> 24:05.193
driving me crazy.

24:06.111 --> 24:07.237
-Oh my.
-Oh no.

24:07.320 --> 24:09.531
I usually don't get drunk easily.

24:10.282 --> 24:11.533
You'll hurt yourself.

24:11.616 --> 24:14.035
Just lift your foot a little. Yes.

24:15.745 --> 24:17.372
You sound just like my dad.

24:17.456 --> 24:19.458
What was that sound you just made?

24:20.041 --> 24:20.959
Are you bleeding?

24:22.586 --> 24:23.712
I think it's a cut.

24:24.963 --> 24:26.840
I think we need to apply pressure.

24:27.841 --> 24:29.551
It's not bleeding though.

24:33.472 --> 24:34.389
Preemptive steps.

24:45.066 --> 24:45.984
How can this be?

24:47.319 --> 24:50.697
I feel like I'm about to drop dead…

24:56.703 --> 24:57.704
"Drop dead"?

25:11.343 --> 25:15.096
When I used to carry those books for you,

25:16.348 --> 25:17.807
I kept thinking,

25:19.351 --> 25:21.603
"I want to hold her hand."

25:23.813 --> 25:25.106
But we were…

25:25.607 --> 25:26.691
See?

25:27.817 --> 25:29.194
This is why I said,

25:29.277 --> 25:32.489
"Everyone has a dark side, after all."

25:33.073 --> 25:34.658
…no longer innocent.

25:35.617 --> 25:37.452
I think I've gone to the darker side.

25:45.710 --> 25:48.630
We dated like grown-ups…

25:52.175 --> 25:54.719
more like La-Z-Boy than IKEA.

26:20.328 --> 26:21.830
Are you out of your mind?

26:23.248 --> 26:25.500
What's with your face? And your hands?

26:27.252 --> 26:30.547
Come on. Stop making that face.

26:30.630 --> 26:34.718
Come on. Are you drawing me
like they did in Titanic?

26:35.760 --> 26:39.556
Come on. How can I draw you
like they did in Titanic?

26:39.639 --> 26:42.017
The model is different,
and so is the situation.

26:42.517 --> 26:43.685
"The situation"?

26:46.146 --> 26:47.772
Well, what should the situation be?

26:47.856 --> 26:49.065
Wow.

26:49.149 --> 26:50.692
-Come on, Park Toto.
-"Park Toto"?

26:50.775 --> 26:52.777
Then what should the situation be?

26:53.778 --> 26:56.197
Toto keeps going to the dark side, huh?

27:01.995 --> 27:03.288
God, seriously.

27:03.788 --> 27:06.791
Come on. How could you spit on my face?

27:08.043 --> 27:09.586
Stop calling me Park Toto!

27:09.669 --> 27:14.215
Why do you like Park Toto so much?
I thought you never laughed at anything.

27:14.299 --> 27:16.259
Toto and I shared the same sense of humor.

27:16.343 --> 27:19.429
You're rubbing off on me.
I'm starting to talk like you too.

27:20.013 --> 27:22.641
In a grown-up world
where we learned to fake smiles,

27:22.724 --> 27:24.517
it was an incredible booster.

27:24.601 --> 27:27.312
Don't make me laugh while we're kissing.

27:27.395 --> 27:28.688
I can't focus.

27:29.189 --> 27:32.609
Babe, it's harder
to laugh together every day

27:32.692 --> 27:35.612
than it is to kiss every day.

27:35.695 --> 27:37.489
That's why we're a good match.

27:37.572 --> 27:39.574
-Don't add garlic for now.
-Okay.

27:41.701 --> 27:44.829
Do you really like raw fish?

27:44.913 --> 27:46.039
You always eat it.

27:46.665 --> 27:47.707
Yeah, I do.

27:51.252 --> 27:53.713
Hey, do you want to eat

27:55.006 --> 27:56.549
some real amberjack?

27:57.926 --> 27:59.260
-Real amberjack?
-Yeah.

28:00.011 --> 28:01.262
Real amberjack.

28:05.016 --> 28:06.184
And finally…

28:11.731 --> 28:14.401
Finally, the two men met.

28:18.446 --> 28:19.280
Darn it.

28:20.615 --> 28:24.160
Amberjack, my foot.
Where did this damn saury come from?

28:32.627 --> 28:33.628
Hey, Dad.

28:34.295 --> 28:39.008
Why are you looking at him like that?
You'll make my man uncomfortable.

28:39.718 --> 28:43.054
The day came when I sided
with my man over my old man.

28:45.598 --> 28:47.350
This is how I look at people.

28:48.059 --> 28:51.104
Try to look at him with some kindness.

28:51.187 --> 28:53.815
Being on a boat isn't easy
for someone from the land.

28:53.898 --> 28:55.692
Was it easy for you from the get-go?

28:55.775 --> 28:57.068
-Yeah.
-Yeah, right.

28:59.404 --> 29:02.490
Are you letting them go
because they're still too small?

29:02.574 --> 29:04.242
You're such a kind fisherman.

29:04.909 --> 29:05.994
Your father

29:07.036 --> 29:07.996
is so kind.

29:08.830 --> 29:11.750
They're bait.
We're throwing them to their deaths.

29:14.002 --> 29:15.378
Not so kind now, huh?

29:16.504 --> 29:20.550
Come on, stop glaring at him
and catch me an amberjack.

29:21.050 --> 29:23.762
I brought him here
to eat some real amberjack.

29:39.527 --> 29:41.321
Why do you keep following her?

29:41.404 --> 29:43.072
Why? She's just going to the toilet.

29:43.865 --> 29:47.535
Just sit and eat some amberjack.
And pay for what you eat.

29:48.953 --> 29:49.954
AUNTIES' SEAFOOD HOUSE

29:50.038 --> 29:51.664
Rice cakes for sale!

29:54.626 --> 29:56.002
Rice cakes for sale!

29:56.085 --> 29:58.797
IMF CRISIS, HALF PRICE FOR JEJU CITIZENS
LET'S EAT AND SURVIVE TOGETHER

29:58.880 --> 30:00.840
Rice cakes for sale!

30:00.924 --> 30:04.219
Someone, buy her rice cakes.
Why won't anyone buy her rice cakes?

30:06.679 --> 30:08.723
Rice cakes for sale!

30:08.807 --> 30:11.643
GATHER THE GOLD IN OUR CLOSETS
TO REVIVE THE NATION'S ECONOMY

30:13.770 --> 30:15.730
Rice cakes for sale!

30:15.814 --> 30:19.526
Are they playing a game
where the first one to speak loses?

30:39.170 --> 30:40.630
GOLD COLLECTION CAMPAIGN PARTICIPANTS

30:40.713 --> 30:43.716
But why aren't you sitting over there?
Why do you ignore them?

30:43.800 --> 30:45.093
Maybe she doesn't like him.

30:46.219 --> 30:48.930
You don't? What do you think of him?

30:50.557 --> 30:51.683
Me?

30:57.105 --> 31:00.108
Get your head off my shoulder!

31:00.984 --> 31:03.486
So why are you here?
Why did you come to Jeju?

31:03.570 --> 31:06.573
Are you playing 20 Questions or what?

31:06.656 --> 31:08.825
I told you not to be like that.

31:10.118 --> 31:12.579
You can't talk, ride boats,
or even drink, huh?

31:12.662 --> 31:16.624
Why should I give my daughter to you?
Would you, if you were me?

31:16.708 --> 31:19.294
I'm angry for absolutely no reason.

31:19.377 --> 31:22.088
But even now, you're not even trying.

31:23.214 --> 31:25.675
Even if I wanted to impress you,

31:26.551 --> 31:28.803
if you don't like me…

31:30.889 --> 31:32.557
no matter what I do--

31:32.640 --> 31:35.435
He won't like you in any case,
so you won't even try to suck up?

31:35.518 --> 31:36.811
Who do you think you are?

31:36.895 --> 31:38.855
You little brat. You're so damn rude.

31:39.439 --> 31:40.315
Let go.

31:40.815 --> 31:42.150
Ten, nine, eight--

31:42.233 --> 31:44.319
Seven, six, five, four,
three, two, one. What?

31:44.402 --> 31:45.653
I said let go.

31:59.208 --> 32:00.627
What do you think of him?

32:01.711 --> 32:02.629
Well,

32:03.755 --> 32:04.672
you know…

32:06.174 --> 32:07.675
You have something to say?

32:07.759 --> 32:09.969
If you do, just say it. Come on.

32:10.762 --> 32:11.971
Here's the thing.

32:13.598 --> 32:14.599
His family…

32:17.393 --> 32:18.811
You know, his family…

32:24.275 --> 32:25.109
I mean,

32:26.486 --> 32:29.197
I'm doing whatever I can to impress you.

32:29.280 --> 32:30.448
What did you do?

32:30.531 --> 32:33.242
I haven't noticed a thing this whole time.

32:35.370 --> 32:37.038
I normally don't eat much, but…

32:39.040 --> 32:41.084
Sorry for preparing too much food.

32:41.584 --> 32:43.086
Watch it.

32:43.586 --> 32:46.339
I'm this close to actually beating you up.

32:47.674 --> 32:49.092
Don't glare at me.

32:59.727 --> 33:03.648
Why are you getting up again?
Why keep following her to the toilet?

33:03.731 --> 33:05.066
What are you trying to do?

33:05.149 --> 33:07.026
What are you going to do in the dark?

33:07.110 --> 33:08.319
You'll be dead meat.

33:08.987 --> 33:11.155
It's dark, so I have to--

33:11.239 --> 33:13.783
Attention!

33:13.866 --> 33:15.952
It's dark, so I'll…

33:18.079 --> 33:18.913
It's cold, so…

33:26.087 --> 33:27.714
Why the hell is that punk so stiff?

33:27.797 --> 33:30.091
What if Yang likes him
more than he likes her?

33:31.926 --> 33:34.470
No, what if my sister
is making a fuss over nothing--

33:34.554 --> 33:36.597
Did you just call
your brother-in-law "punk"?

33:36.681 --> 33:38.599
"Brother-in-law"? So you approve of him?

33:38.683 --> 33:41.185
You selfish kid.
Don't eat all the shrimp by yourself.

33:41.269 --> 33:42.645
Peel a few for him!

33:43.229 --> 33:45.106
Wait, why? What is it about him?

33:45.732 --> 33:46.649
Seriously, why?

33:47.358 --> 33:48.276
My God.

33:56.743 --> 33:59.579
Why do you keep following her?
Why? She's just going to the toilet.

34:00.163 --> 34:03.750
Just sit and eat some amberjack.
And pay for what you eat.

34:05.043 --> 34:06.919
Good grief, why do you keep…

34:08.671 --> 34:09.839
In case she falls.

34:10.590 --> 34:12.592
In case Geum-myeong falls.

34:12.675 --> 34:16.095
You think I'd let my daughter fall
into the water?

34:17.013 --> 34:19.390
You should worry about yourself.
Hey, attention.

34:20.641 --> 34:21.601
Attention!

34:24.020 --> 34:25.980
Still, I should protect her, so…

34:28.107 --> 34:29.400
I'm worried, so…

34:41.746 --> 34:43.414
I don't stand a chance.

34:44.582 --> 34:46.626
How am I supposed to impress him?

35:09.190 --> 35:10.358
You know what, babe?

35:12.318 --> 35:13.903
You were a bit stiff in there.

35:15.029 --> 35:16.030
Well,

35:17.907 --> 35:19.075
I want to impress him,

35:20.243 --> 35:23.996
but this is just how I am, and--

35:24.622 --> 35:27.333
So that's just how you are.

35:27.834 --> 35:30.419
I don't know what I'm supposed to do.

35:31.462 --> 35:33.714
It's hard to do things I never do, so--

35:33.798 --> 35:37.718
So you think I'm the kind of person
who normally sucks up to others

35:37.802 --> 35:41.430
and changes my voice around your mother
just because that's who I am?

35:44.642 --> 35:46.727
Let me be clear. I'm…

35:46.811 --> 35:48.062
-Are you listening?
-Yes.

35:48.146 --> 35:50.815
I am my dad's daughter.

35:50.898 --> 35:54.110
If my dad says no, that's a no for me too.

35:56.279 --> 35:57.780
-No wedding bells.
-Babe.

35:58.865 --> 35:59.866
Babe.

36:04.704 --> 36:06.372
Wait, why do you approve of him?

36:08.166 --> 36:10.710
Then why didn't you approve of my wife
from the get-go?

36:10.793 --> 36:13.921
I won't stand anyone
treating my Hyeon-suk differently.

36:14.005 --> 36:15.840
Go away. Just go.

36:15.923 --> 36:19.510
Hey, does your Hyeon-suk know
you pooped your pants in kindergarten?

36:19.594 --> 36:22.388
Does your Chung-seop know
you used my razor?

36:24.098 --> 36:26.225
-Let go of me.
-Father!

36:33.107 --> 36:34.108
Oh my.

36:35.484 --> 36:36.736
Father.

36:37.445 --> 36:38.696
Father!

36:39.989 --> 36:42.783
Is it okay for me

36:42.867 --> 36:44.785
to peel some shrimp for you?

36:45.620 --> 36:46.913
Peel them for yourself.

36:48.206 --> 36:49.582
He gets weird when he's drunk.

36:55.880 --> 36:57.757
Look at him.

36:57.840 --> 37:00.509
He absolutely adores Geum-myeong.

37:02.094 --> 37:05.806
But you know,
his mom really wants Geum-myeong too.

37:06.307 --> 37:08.935
She says she's really fond of Geum-myeong.

37:09.018 --> 37:10.478
Isn't it funny?

37:11.103 --> 37:13.064
Yep, it's so funny. It sure is.

37:13.147 --> 37:14.690
You cried, didn't you?

37:15.191 --> 37:16.192
Why would I?

37:17.068 --> 37:19.195
Who in the world
wouldn't love our Geum-myeong?

37:20.029 --> 37:20.947
You cried.

37:21.030 --> 37:23.699
This is really wild honey
from Hallasan, right?

37:24.283 --> 37:26.911
You're going to give this to his mom,
aren't you?

37:26.994 --> 37:28.579
Well, you know,

37:29.413 --> 37:33.542
Chung-seop's mom gave me a gift first.

37:34.669 --> 37:36.879
She practically bribed me.

37:36.963 --> 37:39.382
Not everyone would do that.

37:40.341 --> 37:43.552
You know what I got yesterday?

37:44.053 --> 37:46.931
What is this, some kind of treasure?

37:47.014 --> 37:47.974
What could it be

37:49.433 --> 37:50.768
that she'd pack so tightly?

37:50.851 --> 37:52.520
Why are we letting him sleep here?

37:52.603 --> 37:54.522
We should just get him a room at an inn.

37:55.231 --> 37:57.817
How can we tell him to sleep at an inn?

37:57.900 --> 38:00.736
I feel bad enough
that he has to sleep in the living room.

38:00.820 --> 38:03.990
How can I sleep
under the same roof as Park Chung-seop?

38:04.073 --> 38:05.574
Why can't you sleep?

38:05.658 --> 38:07.159
I just can't.

38:07.994 --> 38:11.539
Seriously, stop going out to check him.

38:11.622 --> 38:14.458
He's not going to sneak
into Geum-myeong's room.

38:14.542 --> 38:17.044
How can he
when you're glaring at him like that?

38:17.628 --> 38:18.546
Don't!

38:18.629 --> 38:19.588
Let me go. Hey.

38:21.382 --> 38:23.551
Just sit down! Goodness!

38:48.200 --> 38:51.579
Father, why do you keep coming out here
instead of going to sleep?

38:51.662 --> 38:53.497
What about you? Why aren't you sleeping?

38:54.081 --> 38:56.000
Why not? What is it?

38:56.083 --> 38:57.585
What are you going to do?

38:58.085 --> 39:01.422
What? What's wrong? Is there a problem?

39:14.143 --> 39:17.563
I went home in the fall,
picked the best persimmons.

39:17.646 --> 39:22.276
I put in effort all season long,
thinking of giving them to you.

39:23.277 --> 39:28.157
I made these, looking at them every day,
just like gazing at lovely Geum-myeong.

39:28.657 --> 39:32.536
That's how fond I am of Geum-myeong.

39:32.620 --> 39:33.788
FROM CHUNG-SEOP'S MOM

39:33.871 --> 39:35.414
Perhaps Mom

39:35.998 --> 39:39.710
had been waiting for a long time
to hear those words.

39:42.338 --> 39:43.881
Gonna stand watch all night?

39:44.673 --> 39:47.510
And just what will you do
if he goes into Geum-myeong's room?

39:49.762 --> 39:50.930
He'll be dead meat.

39:53.641 --> 39:55.559
What can you do?

39:55.643 --> 39:58.604
Has Geum-myeong's dad
ever once won against her?

40:03.150 --> 40:04.735
Let her go now.

40:06.529 --> 40:07.822
Your uneven love.

40:12.118 --> 40:13.244
Mom knew…

40:18.374 --> 40:20.292
that this would happen eventually.

40:21.502 --> 40:24.130
Single Bungle Show!
I'm your host, Kang Seok.

40:24.880 --> 40:27.633
The IMF crisis brought about
many gloomy terms, didn't it?

40:27.716 --> 40:29.593
"MUTT."
Most are Unemployed in Their Twenties.

40:29.677 --> 40:30.511
STORE CLOSING SALE

40:30.594 --> 40:32.721
"The 38th Parallel."
If you're 38, you must resign.

40:32.805 --> 40:35.850
"RAFFLE."
Retire At Forty-Five Like Everyone Else."

40:35.933 --> 40:38.894
"Job thief."
Working until 56 makes you a thief.

40:39.562 --> 40:41.522
It truly is a world without smiles.

40:42.022 --> 40:44.900
Well, let's listen to an uplifting song.

40:50.906 --> 40:53.617
Just like that, I leapt from the nest.

41:03.878 --> 41:06.672
Like a bluebird soaring
above a bare mountain,

41:06.755 --> 41:08.299
fluttering with excitement

41:09.842 --> 41:11.343
and brimming with confidence.

41:12.303 --> 41:13.762
Don't smile too much today.

41:14.847 --> 41:15.973
It'll annoy your father.

41:18.017 --> 41:19.768
Mom, don't do that today.

41:19.852 --> 41:21.604
Don't cry like this, okay?

41:24.064 --> 41:24.899
Come on.

41:24.982 --> 41:27.276
Are you done with me once I'm married?

41:27.359 --> 41:28.486
You won't be my mom?

41:28.986 --> 41:30.279
Listen to me.

41:30.362 --> 41:33.657
I'll still be Yang Geum-myeong,
not Park Geum-myeong.

41:34.241 --> 41:36.994
What are the last digits of my pager?
Not his home number, right?

41:37.077 --> 41:38.913
It’s still our family's 3312, right?

41:39.538 --> 41:41.832
Then which family would I belong to?

41:42.333 --> 41:45.044
I know. I'm not giving my daughter away.

41:45.753 --> 41:47.546
So don't cry.

41:48.047 --> 41:49.507
If you cry, I'll cry.

41:49.590 --> 41:51.634
All the wedding photos will be ruined.

41:55.095 --> 41:57.223
Let's keep it nice and cool.

41:58.057 --> 41:59.058
Okay?

42:43.602 --> 42:47.273
Oh dear! How did you make it here?

42:47.356 --> 42:49.400
How could I miss
your family's celebration?

42:49.483 --> 42:51.068
The girl who's getting married…

42:51.151 --> 42:52.278
Can you straighten this?

42:52.361 --> 42:54.697
…is the one who loved caramel, isn't she?

42:54.780 --> 42:58.284
Yes, it's Geum-myeong.
You always gave her free caramel.

43:00.411 --> 43:01.912
Yes, go ahead, please.

43:05.499 --> 43:07.001
Wow, you look pretty today.

43:10.671 --> 43:12.381
-Hey, where's Ju-gyeong?
-Ju-gyeong?

43:12.464 --> 43:15.509
-How can the photographer be late?
-There she is.

43:16.427 --> 43:17.303
-Hey!
-Hey!

43:30.357 --> 43:31.567
I shouldn't have come.

43:33.027 --> 43:34.028
-Ju-gyeong!
-Hey!

43:34.111 --> 43:35.654
-Hey!
-Hurry!

43:35.738 --> 43:37.072
Come on, hurry.

43:37.990 --> 43:38.824
Hey, hurry.

43:42.494 --> 43:43.412
What was that?

43:45.289 --> 43:47.041
She looks so damn beautiful.

43:48.042 --> 43:50.044
Hey, the photographer can't be late.

43:50.127 --> 43:52.379
You should've started snapping
when I got out of the car.

43:52.463 --> 43:55.049
Are you happy? You're one confident bride.

43:58.302 --> 44:00.929
-Come on.
-Start taking pictures of me from here.

44:01.013 --> 44:01.847
Okay.

44:04.725 --> 44:05.559
So pretty.

44:05.643 --> 44:06.727
Let's go over there.

44:06.810 --> 44:07.728
Go to the steps.

44:07.811 --> 44:08.771
Those steps.

44:08.854 --> 44:12.566
Does everyone marry
their most passionate love?

44:13.817 --> 44:17.529
The size of the love wasn't different.
Its temperature was.

44:17.613 --> 44:20.199
You sent us so many tangerines.

44:20.282 --> 44:22.618
You never have to buy
another tangerine again.

44:22.701 --> 44:25.287
It was the temperature
that let me be myself.

44:27.039 --> 44:28.123
Did you say hello?

44:29.333 --> 44:32.294
I've found my prince.

44:52.189 --> 44:53.857
What a match made in heaven.

44:53.941 --> 44:56.110
Did you teach him to be cringy,
or is it him?

44:56.193 --> 44:57.653
He's my top student.

44:58.612 --> 45:00.239
How lovely.

45:05.327 --> 45:07.371
Next, the groom will enter.

45:09.456 --> 45:12.376
The groom is making a confident entrance.

45:12.459 --> 45:15.003
Please welcome him
with a round of applause.

45:26.348 --> 45:29.893
Did I not say I hate it
when brides cry at their weddings?

45:30.561 --> 45:31.979
Don't you dare cry, Dad.

45:32.062 --> 45:34.022
If you cry, I'll really get annoyed.

45:34.106 --> 45:35.941
Never mind. You know what?

45:36.024 --> 45:38.402
Just try not to look me in the eye, okay?

45:42.448 --> 45:43.449
Geum-myeong.

45:45.784 --> 45:46.994
You can do well, right?

45:47.786 --> 45:51.081
If things go wrong, back down.
Just run straight to me, okay?

45:51.165 --> 45:52.082
Okay?

46:00.174 --> 46:01.592
Can you really eat this?

46:02.384 --> 46:04.344
If you don't like it, back down.

46:04.845 --> 46:06.221
Just spit it out, okay?

46:11.685 --> 46:12.686
Goodness.

46:14.146 --> 46:15.147
YANG GEUM-MYEONG

46:16.690 --> 46:17.691
Do these fit?

46:25.199 --> 46:27.701
Say, "Hello, teacher."

46:27.785 --> 46:29.828
Hello, teacher.

46:31.079 --> 46:32.164
Goodness me.

46:33.832 --> 46:36.418
I'm telling you,
we can't send her to school yet.

46:36.919 --> 46:38.462
Let's just send her next year.

46:38.545 --> 46:41.840
You want to keep her at home forever?

46:42.549 --> 46:44.092
How will you ever marry her off?

46:44.176 --> 46:46.178
You're being so silly. Isn't he silly?

46:46.261 --> 46:48.722
Geum-myeong,
you think you can go to school?

46:49.389 --> 46:52.309
I can. Jeong-geun went too.

46:52.392 --> 46:54.186
What does it matter if he went?

46:54.269 --> 46:56.563
I don't like you being close
with Jeong-geun.

46:56.647 --> 46:58.023
I want to go to school.

47:00.901 --> 47:04.905
Then go for now,
and if you don't like it, back down.

47:05.572 --> 47:08.450
Just run straight home, okay?
I'll be at home.

47:08.534 --> 47:09.868
-All right?
-Okay.

47:15.123 --> 47:18.168
Geum-myeong,
you can run well tomorrow, right?

47:18.669 --> 47:20.128
I think I might come in first.

47:20.212 --> 47:21.213
First place?

47:21.839 --> 47:23.382
-Ready… That's not it.
-Go!

47:23.465 --> 47:24.633
Run at "Go," okay?

47:25.259 --> 47:28.804
But you don't have to come first.
Back down if you want.

47:29.304 --> 47:33.392
If you fall, just run straight to me.
I'll be right behind you tomorrow. Okay?

47:33.475 --> 47:34.393
Okay.

47:34.476 --> 47:36.019
-Ready--
-Go!

47:37.688 --> 47:38.897
Oh dear.

47:39.398 --> 47:41.316
YOU CAN EASILY SCORE HIGH!

47:44.194 --> 47:46.196
COLLEGE ENTRANCE EXAM IDENTIFICATION SLIP

47:46.280 --> 47:48.574
Come on!

47:48.657 --> 47:49.783
You got this!

47:50.868 --> 47:52.536
Let's go, Munil High School!

47:53.453 --> 47:55.289
We're here way too early again.

47:56.373 --> 47:57.374
Seriously.

47:58.041 --> 47:59.918
Why is our family so diligent?

48:00.002 --> 48:03.380
What kind of lives have you led
to be like this?

48:03.463 --> 48:04.464
Geum-myeong.

48:05.299 --> 48:07.092
-You can guess well, right?
-Come on.

48:07.593 --> 48:11.763
Why would I guess the answers?
Dad, I'm Yang Geum-myeong.

48:12.890 --> 48:13.807
You're right.

48:13.891 --> 48:16.602
I know from years of seeing you
that you do everything well.

48:16.685 --> 48:18.812
You're good at everything.
Dad knows that now.

48:19.813 --> 48:23.734
So you'll just say I do everything well?
You won't tell me to back down?

48:24.234 --> 48:28.280
Still, if your head hurts
and you just can't do it, just back down.

48:28.864 --> 48:31.074
Just run straight out.
I'll be right here. Okay?

48:32.492 --> 48:34.036
You're always my backup, huh?

48:34.912 --> 48:39.333
Are you sure you don't need
any herbal calming remedies?

48:44.755 --> 48:45.589
YANG GEUM-MYEONG

48:45.672 --> 48:47.674
THE PRIDE OF DODONG!
MY DAUGHTER WILL GET IN!

48:48.508 --> 48:50.052
Every time I walked the tightrope,

48:51.303 --> 48:54.598
my dad stood there holding the net.

48:56.099 --> 48:57.726
"I'll be there even if you fall."

48:58.936 --> 49:01.563
I wish I had told him

49:03.273 --> 49:04.983
how comforting his words were

49:05.609 --> 49:06.443
at least once.

49:08.487 --> 49:10.489
While he was standing there,

49:11.698 --> 49:14.576
it seemed the snow fell only on my dad.

49:18.246 --> 49:20.832
The bride will now enter
and walk down the aisle.

49:21.333 --> 49:22.167
Geum-myeong.

49:23.251 --> 49:24.086
What?

49:24.169 --> 49:25.504
Dad's still right here.

49:25.587 --> 49:29.800
Just do everything you want.
Whatever you want.

49:31.593 --> 49:33.095
Amid my dad's winter,

49:33.178 --> 49:34.763
I grew into lush green.

49:35.263 --> 49:37.140
Feeding on their verdant youth,

49:38.517 --> 49:39.977
I became a tree.

49:45.983 --> 49:49.736
If Chung-seop annoys you, come back to me.
Dad's always here for you. Okay?

49:50.612 --> 49:55.450
No. Don't say things like that right now.

49:55.951 --> 49:58.328
You're so annoying, Dad.

49:59.788 --> 50:02.124
Please welcome the bride.

50:07.004 --> 50:09.423
Please give her a warm round of applause.

50:34.114 --> 50:36.491
Gwang-rye must be beaming from ear to ear.

50:36.575 --> 50:39.786
She must be so happy at last.

50:43.373 --> 50:46.960
When Ae-sun walked down the aisle
holding her uncle's hand,

50:47.044 --> 50:49.296
I thought I'd just die from heartache.

50:49.796 --> 50:53.550
The daughter's respectable life
felt like a medal to her mother,

50:54.051 --> 50:55.761
so she kept smiling.

50:58.096 --> 51:01.016
In case the bride didn't come
because she was crying,

51:01.099 --> 51:03.060
the groom rushed out to greet her.

51:03.560 --> 51:06.605
Please give them
another big round of applause.

51:13.361 --> 51:16.698
We said we'd keep it cool.
Why are you bawling?

51:25.082 --> 51:28.210
Aren't we getting married?
Should we call it off?

51:30.337 --> 51:32.130
No, I'm going to do it.

51:35.842 --> 51:36.676
Let's go.

51:58.657 --> 52:01.034
It was only the day before my dad left me

52:01.868 --> 52:04.162
that I rushed to pour out apologies,

52:05.914 --> 52:07.874
"Dad, I'm sorry. I'm so sorry."

52:09.918 --> 52:11.419
Dad told me back then

52:12.587 --> 52:14.131
that he had been living in heaven

52:15.340 --> 52:18.093
since the day I was born.

52:29.855 --> 52:30.939
I told you

52:31.439 --> 52:33.567
your father would cry more than your mom.

52:35.485 --> 52:37.571
My dad's crying?

52:52.335 --> 52:54.880
I didn't think
your dad would be like that.

52:55.505 --> 52:58.967
Why do men want to act tough
around their sons-in-law?

52:59.050 --> 53:00.927
Why drink more than he can handle?

53:01.011 --> 53:03.763
Dad wants to see
if he gets weird when he's drunk.

53:03.847 --> 53:06.099
Who's the weird one now?

53:08.685 --> 53:09.853
-Hey, Dad.
-Come on!

53:15.859 --> 53:17.110
What about your mom?

53:18.195 --> 53:19.029
Sorry?

53:19.112 --> 53:20.906
Does she like Geum-myeong or not?

53:21.823 --> 53:26.661
My mother has always been harping on
about wanting a daughter,

53:27.579 --> 53:29.789
so she likes Geum-myeong more than me.

53:29.873 --> 53:30.832
No.

53:32.250 --> 53:34.878
-I'm sorry?
-She's my daughter, not your family's.

53:35.754 --> 53:37.505
She's my daughter forever.

53:38.131 --> 53:40.634
Right. Of course.

53:40.717 --> 53:43.261
-Park Chung-seop!
-Yes, Father.

53:43.845 --> 53:46.640
Do you have any idea
what you're taking from me?

53:47.515 --> 53:48.600
Sorry?

53:49.601 --> 53:51.186
I am giving you…

53:53.897 --> 53:56.149
my heaven.

53:57.859 --> 54:00.695
To you, who did absolutely nothing for her

54:00.779 --> 54:03.698
throughout her 30 years of life.

54:05.784 --> 54:06.618
Well,

54:07.369 --> 54:10.205
I heard that Mother was the literary one.

54:15.794 --> 54:16.795
Hey, Yang Heaven.

54:17.545 --> 54:18.588
Carry your own honey.

54:21.925 --> 54:25.845
Dad had his uneven love stolen away
just like that.

54:26.805 --> 54:30.767
We now ask the bride and groom
to face the bride's parents.

54:38.525 --> 54:42.195
Bride and groom,
please bow to the bride's parents.

54:54.416 --> 54:58.169
Oh dear, the bride's father is crying.
My goodness!

54:58.253 --> 54:59.379
Be quiet.

54:59.462 --> 55:02.549
The bride's father
must've truly loved his daughter.

55:02.632 --> 55:05.468
Gwan-sik is being robbed
of his most precious treasure.

55:05.552 --> 55:07.429
He's being robbed of it!

55:07.512 --> 55:10.515
He wouldn't cry like that
even if his mother got remarried.

55:14.728 --> 55:16.813
I wish you well. Go on.

55:18.481 --> 55:21.651
Next, the bride and groom
will bow to the groom's mother.

55:22.902 --> 55:24.696
Enough is enough, okay?

55:27.407 --> 55:29.451
You're so embarrassing, seriously.

55:30.201 --> 55:33.538
Bride and groom,
please bow to the groom's mother.

55:47.886 --> 55:48.720
Who is it?

55:49.596 --> 55:50.889
Who's looking for you?

55:52.015 --> 55:52.932
Who is this?

55:53.641 --> 55:54.768
I don't know either.

55:56.394 --> 56:00.315
Didn't I tell you to dye your gray hair
before going?

56:01.608 --> 56:03.735
Geum-myeong nagged me about it again.

56:04.235 --> 56:09.783
Obviously, I'd take better care
of my own husband than she would, right?

56:10.533 --> 56:13.453
She's got her husband to look after now.

56:18.583 --> 56:21.628
Life never allows us
to truly savor these moments.

56:23.963 --> 56:24.964
Yang Eun-myeong.

56:31.429 --> 56:32.389
Me?

56:33.139 --> 56:37.018
Happiness comes right at you.
Misfortune always creeps up from behind.

56:37.519 --> 56:38.853
Where is Park Cheol-yong?

56:39.687 --> 56:40.522
You know, right?

56:42.649 --> 56:43.483
Me?

56:47.362 --> 56:49.739
When Mom says
not to hang out with a certain friend,

56:51.366 --> 56:52.951
there's always a good reason.

59:36.781 --> 59:43.329
"IF YOU CAN'T, JUST BACK DOWN.
WE'RE ALWAYS HERE FOR YOU."

59:50.545 --> 59:52.672
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
